What it does: Points an alias domain (subdomain) to another domain name, rather than an IP. The resolver must perform a second lookup on the target domain.

The Analogy: A forwarding address. Instead of listing an address for your pop-up shop, you say: "Our shop is inside the Shopify Shopping Mall."

sneakerhub.com Setup: You want shop.sneakerhub.com to point to your Shopify store without having to manage Shopify's changing IP addresses.

Plaintext
shop.sneakerhub.com.    3600    IN    CNAME    shops.myshopify.com.
Important Rule: You cannot put a CNAME on a root apex domain (sneakerhub.com), only on subdomains (shop.sneakerhub.com, [www.sneakerhub.com](https://www.sneakerhub.com)).
